Cowboy Cookies
  --@bdylanhollis

1 c pecans
1 c coconut
2 c rolled oats
1 c butter
1 c sugar
1 c brown sugar
2 eggs
1 tsp vanilla
2 c flour
1 tsp baking soda
2 c chocolate chips

Toast pecans, coconut, and oats in a 350F oven for 8 min. In a mixing bowl, cream butter and sugars until light and fluffy. Add eggs and vanilla and cream. Add flour and baking soda and mix to combine. Fold in pecans, coconut, oats, and chocolate chips. Scoop out onto sheet and bake for ~11 min at 350F.



GF variation
  --Nicole Hunn

1 1/2 c (210 g) ap gluten free flour blend, (eg. Better Batter)
1/2 tsp xanthan gum, (omit if your blend already contains it)
1 tsp baking powder
1 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp kosher salt
1 1/2 tsp ground cinnamon
1/2 c (100 g) granulated sugar
1 c (218 g) packed light brown sugar
1 1/2 c (150 g) certified gluten free old fashioned rolled oats
1 1/2 c (120 g) coconut chips, (See Recipe Notes)
10 tbsp (140 g) unsalted butter, at room temp
2 (100 g (weighed out of shell)) eggs, at room temperature, beaten
1 1/2 tsp vanilla
8 oz semi-sweet chocolate chips

Preheat your oven to 325F. Line rimmed baking sheets with unbleached parchment paper and set them aside. In a large bowl, place the flour, xanthan gum, baking powder, baking soda, salt, cinnamon, and granulated sugar, and whisk to combine well. Add the brown sugar and mix to combine, working out any lumps in the brown sugar. Add the oats and coconut chips and mix to combine. Create a well in the center of the dry ingredients and add the butter, eggs, and vanilla, mixing to combine after each addition. Press the back of your mixing spoon into the dough to moisten all of the dry ingredients and create a cohesive dough. Add the chocolate chips, and mix until they’re evenly distributed throughout the dough. If necessary to bring the dough together, knead it with your hands. Divide the dough into 20 pieces, each ~2 oz. Roll each into a ball and place ~2" apart on the prepared baking sheets. Flatten each ball into a disk ~1/4" thick. Place the baking sheets in the center of the preheated oven, one at a time, and bake until lightly golden brown all over (~12 min). Remove from the oven and allow to cool on the baking sheet for ~5 min or until firm before transferring to a wire rack to cool completely.

Notes: for more flavor, toast coconut chips - Place them on a rimmed baking sheet in a single even layer, and then in a 300F oven for 10 min or until the chips are beginning to brown on the edges. Add nuts

